From fd7b666cbc3a7e2bf0cfc52f32883d5bf721c7d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hectorqin <14220132+hectorqin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:48:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(plugins): let plugin UIs archive or delete projects
 and sessions

Plugin tabs and tool renderers get archiveProject(path),
deleteProject(path), archiveSession(id) and deleteSession(id) on their
host API. They make the same requests as the sidebar's archive (hide,
keep sessions) and delete (also sessions and transcripts), under the
signed-in user, then refresh the sidebar. Plugins name projects by path,
which is what they know; the host resolves the project id and only acts
on projects it knows to be git worktrees, so a plugin can never remove a
repository's own project. Session actions cover agents that share a
project with other sessions. Outside the project workspace the actions
report that they are unavailable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
